<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia Jan manufacturing input prices rise.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia Jan manufacturing input prices rise.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's manufacturing input prices rose 1.3 percent in January from the previous month, and were 4.6 percent lower than a year before, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.  </p>
<p>    INPUT PRICES (pct change)   Jan	  Dec	  Yr/Yr</p>
<p>    Imported materials	   +0.5	 -0.4	  -8.7</p>
<p>    Domestic materials	   +1.9	 -0.1	  -2.0</p>
<p>    Manufacturing prices	 +1.3	 -0.2	  -4.6</p>
<p>The bureau said price increases for crude oil, sheep and lamb, milk and wheat all contributed to the rise. The biggest fall was in cattle prices.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
